    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so it's just a matter of waiting for the TTL to expire then? i'm just worried because some of the nodes are showing the new IP but others are just... stuck. it feels like the data is just disappearing or getting lost somewhere in the middle. is there anything actually happening in the background that could cause it to be so inconsistent?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The inconsistency you see is typical because different recursive DNS servers around the world have different caching times based on the Time To Live (TTL) set on your old record. Nothing is truly \"lost\"; rather, different ISPs are querying different, up-to-date, or stale copies of the DNS record simultaneously. As the TTL for the old record expires across various points, they will begin querying your authoritative server for the new IP.",
      "source": "target",
